    "result_text": "The `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The full suite is green.\n\nThe change is complete. Here's a summary of what I implemented so the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` derivation works end-to-end:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (source of the generated DTOs):\n   - Added `birthDate` (ISO `date`, optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema \u2014 the input.\n   - Added `ageBand` (readOnly enum `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema \u2014 the derived output.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `birth_date` column) field with getter/setter so the value MapStruct maps from the request survives to DTO derivation.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on the `hsqldb` profile.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added an `ageBand(owner)` derivation, wired via `@Mapping`, computing the age as `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()`: `<18 \u2192 MINOR`, `18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT`, `\u226565 \u2192 SENIOR`. It returns `null` (field absent) when no `birthDate` was supplied, matching the spec's \"when present\" wording. The age is measured against `registrationDate` as required, and MapStruct auto-maps `birthDate` from the request DTO into the entity by name.\n\nThe `coreDerivesAgeBand` acceptance test (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
